        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(doctor): pass collectModelsMap for agents.list model ref scan",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where `openclaw doctor --fix` silently skips scanning legacy Codex model refs (`openai-codex/*`) in `agents.list.<id>.models.*` entries, causing incomplete migration warnings and potentially skipped repair.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\n`collectConfigModelRefs` calls `collectAgentModelRefs` twice: once for `agents.defaults` (with `collectModelsMap: true`) and once for each `agents.list` entry (without `collectModelsMap`). The `collectModelsMap` parameter controls whether the agent's `models` map is scanned for legacy `openai-codex/*` model refs. The list-agent call was missing the parameter, making those entries invisible to the warning generator and the repair early-return gate.\r\n\r\nThe actual repair logic (`rewriteConfigModelRefsWithCompactionPolicy`) already handles list agents correctly. This fix only affects the detection/warning path, which also gates the early return in `maybeRepairCodexRoutes`.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nUsers with legacy Codex model refs only in `agents.list.<name>.models.<ref>` (not in `agents.defaults.models`) will now see accurate doctor warnings and have their config correctly repaired by `openclaw doctor --fix`.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- **One-line change**: add `collectModelsMap: true` to the `collectAgentModelRefs` call in the `agents.list` loop, matching the `agents.defaults` call on line 119.\r\n- **Type check**: `pnpm tsgo:core` passes.\r\n- **Formatting**: `oxfmt` passes.\r\n- **No test regressions**: existing test suite continues to pass.\r\n\r\nCo-Authored-By: Claude\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/bug-007-collectModelsMap-list-agents-missing",
